note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR GPL-2.0-only
note mqput: copy a sealed message (agpu_rpc_seal) into GSP's command queue ring.
note The command queue is the 256 KiB region GSP reads: a 4096-byte header page (msgqTxHeader:
note version 0, size 4, msgSize 8, msgCount 12, writePtr 16, flags 20, rxHdrOff 24, entryOff 28) and
note 63 slots of 4096 bytes from offset 4096. GSP's read pointer lives in GSP's own queue (SWAP_RX);
note the kernel reads it (READ_ONCE) and passes it as gsprd.
note This unit writes the slots only. It returns the new write pointer; the kernel then issues the
note store fence and publishes it at offset 16 (message_queue_cpu.c:574-576), then notifies GSP
note (GSP QUEUE_HEAD(0) = 0). Oracle: aienux c9678d7b gsp_mq_send (tests/host/parity_mq.c).
note Result: new write pointer 0..62, or 1000000 plus: 1 a ring pointer is 63 or more, 2 queue full,
note 3 element count 0 or more than 16.
fn rd32 m view uchar 262144 o ulong to ulong
a = or ulong get m o shl ulong get m add o 1 8
b = or shl ulong get m add o 2 16 shl ulong get m add o 3 24
ret or a b
end
fn cpslot q edit uchar 262144 slot ulong msg view uchar 65536 e ulong to void
d = add 4096 mul slot 4096
s = mul e 4096
for k ulong 4096
put q add d k get msg add s k
end
end
fn agpu_mq_put q edit uchar 262144 msg view uchar 65536 elems ulong gsprd ulong to ulong
wr = rd32 q 16
if or ge wr 63 ge gsprd 63
ret 1000001
end
if or eq elems 0 gt elems 16
ret 1000003
end
room = rem sub add gsprd 63 add wr 1 63
if lt room elems
ret 1000002
end
for e ulong elems
cpslot q rem add wr e 63 msg e
end
ret rem add wr elems 63
end
